      "muse-spark-1.2-contributor": {
        "model_id": "opencode-go/muse-spark-1.2-contributor",
        "display": "Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor",
        "variants": [
          "max"
        ],
        "note": "\u2b50 SAME RULE AS ox-alpha-free BELOW: the `variants` list is what sets the stall threshold, and without an entry here era resolves variant='default' (120s stall base) and kills a reasoning model mid-think having captured only its banner. muse-spark is reasoning-capable with a 1,048,576-token context, so it will absolutely think longer than 120s on a real bundle. `--variant max` verified accepted 2026-08-26 by running `opencode run -m opencode-go/muse-spark-1.2-contributor --variant max` directly, which printed its `> build \u00b7 muse-spark-1.2-contributor` banner and then the expected answer. Added at the same time as the preset, because a preset without this entry is a reviewer that cannot review."
      },
      "ox-alpha-free": {
        "model_id": "opencode-go/ox-alpha-free",
        "variants": [
          "max"
        ],
        "note": "⭐ THE `variants` LIST IS WHAT SETS THE STALL THRESHOLD, AND WITHOUT IT THIS MODEL CANNOT BE REVIEWED WITH. Measured 2026-08-22: ox-alpha prints its `> build · ox-alpha-free` banner (38 bytes) and then thinks SILENTLY for minutes — observed real review runs of 1m20s and 7m41s. With no map entry era resolves variant='default', whose stall base is 120s, so it was killed at 130s wall having emitted only the banner. Two smoke tests failed that way before the cause was found. `--variant max` is accepted by the model (verified directly) and raises the stall base to 600s. ⛔ The model itself was never the problem: `opencode run` direct answers in 20-23s, both with and without `-f` attach."
      }
    }
  },
